%description:

Tcp.baseMss:invalid -- a base MSS below 88 stops the run with an error.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "at least 88".

The classes: linux (1024, the default, the value of Linux tcp_base_mss), other (another value),
invalid (below 88). The code: TcpConnection::initMtuProbing() checks the value, takes the MTU
of the value as the lower end of the search, and starts an active opener at it.

Host under test: host1, with mtuProbing 2 (precondition). Observation: the error, and the exit
code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.baseMss
%# class: invalid
%# value: 87
%# key: *.host1.tcp.baseMss
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpBaseMssInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.baseMss = 87    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.mtuProbing = 2
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
baseMss must be at least 88, but it is 87
